{
 "_doc": "Pearl's battle music (user 2026-10-25, notes/DECISIONS.md: every unique Gen 4 battle track is Pearl's; with Black 2's music at Rowan's question, a track with a real Black 2 counterpart plays it). patches/battle_music.py installs the Pearl songs named here (sinnoh_music's way: pearl_music.trim) and gives the decomp's src/pearlb2/battle_music_itcm.c its tables. Pearl's rules, from pokediamond: 'eye' = the trainer-class encounter music table (arm9/asm/unk_0204AB0C.s UNK_020F4718, 78 classes; any other class: eye_default, sub_0204AD0C); 'battle' = the class -> encounter table (arm9/asm/unk_02047500.s sub_020475C0 + UNK_020F457E; any other class: battle_default); 'victory' = the battle's victory music by the first opponent's class (overlay 11 ov11_0223D1DC.s, the jump table before SEQ_WINTGYM..; any other class: victory_default; a wild battle: victory_wild); 'wild' = species -> battle music (sub_02047668 + the same table; any other species: wild_default). Pearl also plays trainer music for a double battle against any class but Team Galactic's (not built: no Pearl double battle has a leader, the Elite Four, the Champion or Barry as the opponent). 'unova': what each Pearl track becomes with Black 2's music: a Black 2 song (its real counterpart: the PWT remixes of the Sinnoh Gym Leader and Champion themes; Black 2's own versions of Pearl's lake trio and legendary battles, VS_UMA and VS_DPLEGEND, have the same notes (b2tools/patches/battle_music.py melody(): 1.00), and E_SHIRONA is Pearl's Champion encounter theme (0.97)), 'black2' (Black 2's own choice for that class or Pokemon: its eye-contact theme per class, its trainer, wild and victory songs) or 'pearl' (no counterpart: Pearl's track plays). Pearl's Elite Four battle (SEQ_BA_TENNO) is the Gym Leader theme note for note, so its counterpart is the PWT remix of that theme.",
